RELEASE CHECKLIST — follow these steps for every Android app update.

1. In the Flutter project root, increment the version in pubspec.yaml.
   Example: version: 1.0.1+5
   - The part before + is the user-facing version.
   - The number after + is the Android build number. Increase it for every
     release so Android can install the new APK over the previous version.

2. Generate apkrepo/latest.json from pubspec.yaml:
   python .\apkrepo\versionUpdate.py
   Confirm that apkrepo/latest.json contains the exact version, including +build.

3. Build the release APK from the Flutter project root:
   flutter build apk --release
   Copy the new APK into apkrepo, replacing the previous local copy:
   Copy-Item -Force .\build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-release.apk .\apkrepo\app-release.apk
   Keep the same Android application ID and signing key for upgrades.

4. Commit and push the metadata to the separate apkrepo Git repository
   BEFORE creating a GitHub Release. Releases need an existing commit/tag;
   an empty GitHub repository returns HTTP 422 when creating the first release.
   First publication from the clean-main branch:
   cd .\apkrepo
   git add .gitignore latest.json versionUpdate.py ALWAYS_UPDATE_PUBSEC_YAML_AND_RUN_VERSION_UPDATE
   git commit -m "Add app version metadata"
   git push -u origin clean-main:main

   For later releases, while in apkrepo:
   git add latest.json
   git commit -m "Update app version to 1.0.1+5"
   git push origin HEAD:main

5. Publish the APK as a GitHub Release asset; never commit the APK to Git.
   From inside apkrepo, after the metadata commit has been pushed:
   gh release create "v1.0.1+5" .\app-release.apk --title "v1.0.1+5" --notes "New update 1.0.1+5"
   Use the version you actually released in the tag, title, and notes.
   Keep the asset name exactly app-release.apk. The backend's stable APK URL
   should resolve to the asset on the latest release:
   https://github.com/iimadouu/renolookapk/releases/latest/download/app-release.apk

6. Verify the backend contract before considering the release complete.
   GET https://barberhouse-api.imadedar98.workers.dev/app/latest-version
   It must return HTTP 200 and JSON containing both fields:
   {"version":"1.0.1+5","downloadUrl":"https://github.com/iimadouu/renolookapk/releases/latest/download/app-release.apk"}
   Open the returned downloadUrl and confirm the APK downloads. If the route
   returns 404 or the version is stale, fix/deploy the Worker or publish the
   metadata before expecting the app's launch update check to find the release


Important:
- The app checks the Worker endpoint /app/latest-version at launch. It does
  not read latest.json directly; the Worker reads latest.json and returns the
  version and downloadUrl.
- The app compares version and build number. A higher version/build triggers
  the non-dismissable update dialog; its Update button opens downloadUrl.
- app-release.apk is ignored by apkrepo/.gitignore because regular GitHub Git
  pushes reject files over 100 MB. Upload it to the GitHub Release instead.
